{
  "_comment_declutter": "Heuristic $HOME cleanup (tools/home-declutter.py). Never deletes a live file directly -- `quarantine` moves into quarantine_root, `purge` (the only irreversible step) is always manual, run with --confirm by hand. A candidate is only quarantined once BOTH gates clear: the hardlink guard (every contained file has st_nlink==1, or `find -xdev -samefile` over the roots below finds no sibling) AND recoverability (either it matches a 'regenerable' pattern -- caches, __pycache__, expected to regenerate rather than be restored -- or `garde <path>` confirms an off-machine copy exists). exclude entries are checked before any pattern and are never touched (.git is also always skipped, hardcoded). regenerable.patterns are glob-matched against basenames (files and directories); a matched directory is quarantined whole and not descended into. stale_downloads flags files directly inside its roots older than stale_days matching one of extensions (e.g. old installers already installed) -- these are real content, so they always need garde coverage, never the regenerable shortcut. debris walks its roots recursively (files only, directories are never a whole-tree candidate here) for name-shaped stray-leftover signals -- pre-migration backup suffixes, conflict-resolution snapshot suffixes, temp/tmp-token names, and (independent of name) zero-byte files -- these are real content, not caches, so they always need garde coverage too, same as stale_downloads. debris.roots defaults to a bare '~' here: 2026-08 interactive session with Zach confirmed this debris shape is junk wherever it appears in $HOME, not just in Downloads, and it is bounded by the exclude list above rather than by narrowing roots. Keep regenerable/stale_downloads roots narrow and add them deliberately -- a bare '~' walks every byte under $HOME including any large media/project libraries, which is slow and low-yield for a dev-cache pattern search.",
  "declutter": {
    "quarantine_root": "~/.senechal-quarantine",
    "purge_after_days": 30,
    "exclude": [
      "~/Documents/Projects",
      "~/.cache",
      "~/.local",
      "~/.ssh",
      "~/.gnupg"
    ],
    "regenerable": {
      "roots": [
        "~/Downloads",
        "~/Desktop"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "__pycache__",
        ".pytest_cache",
        "*.tmp",
        "*~",
        "*.bak",
        ".DS_Store"
      ]
    },
    "stale_downloads": {
      "roots": [
        "~/Downloads"
      ],
      "stale_days": 180,
      "extensions": [
        ".deb",
        ".AppImage",
        ".rpm",
        ".dmg",
        ".exe",
        ".msi"
      ]
    },
    "debris": {
      "roots": [
        "~"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "*.pre-*-migration.*",
        "*.pre-*.20*",
        "*.conflicted-snapshot-*",
        "*conflicted*snapshot*"
      ],
      "treat_zero_byte_as_debris": true
    }
  },
  "unused_software": {
    "_comment": "remedies/mandark-unused-software.sh reads this list (lib/common.sh's cfg_unused_software), never hardcodes package names. Each entry is a package a hand-audit confirmed dead by real config/data-directory evidence -- when the app was actually launched last, not just its binary's atime (atime alone produced false positives during the 2026-08-11 audit: dcpomatic/lilypond/openscad/sublime-text all looked stale until their real config dirs were checked -- see MANDARK-APP-MAP.md). kind is 'apt' (removed via `apt-get remove`, configs kept), 'snap' (removed via `snap remove`), or 'localbin' (removed via `rm` of the single file under ~/.local/bin). Add or reclassify an item here, never in the script. The 2026-08-11 Ubuntu Studio sweep deliberately left out several packages with real (if old) evidence of use -- ardour, hydrogen, yoshimi, k3b, hugin, phasex, kid3-qt -- and a few tightly coupled to the JACK audio graph the kept tools (ardour, Pure Data) actually use -- csound (pd-csound depends on it), jack-keyboard, jack-mixer, qjackctl, mcpdisp, xjadeo (ardour-video-timeline recommends it), meterbridge (jackd2/jack-capture reference it). See MANDARK-APP-MAP.md for the full reasoning; none of those are registered here.",
